<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss sight deposits rise to 3,554.7 million Sfr.</title>
<headline>Swiss sight deposits rise to 3,554.7 million Sfr.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss National Bank said sight deposits rose by 461.5 million Swiss francs to 3,554.7 million in the reporting period ended September 30.</p>
<p>Statement of October 1 in millions of Swiss francs:</p>
<p>				    Latest   Change since Sept 20</p>
<p> Sight deposits		 3,554.7  plus	  461.5</p>
<p> Currency reserves	    38,887.2 plus	  60.0</p>
<p> Domestic securities	  3,042.5  minus	 13.7</p>
<p> Notes in circulation	 28,300.1 plus	  806.3</p>
<p> Other call deposits	  422.7    plus	  54.8</p>
<p> Goverment time deposits    1,200.0  minus	 1,150.0</p>
<p>Borrowing at the emergency Lombard window rose by 6.2 million francs to 6.2 million from null in the previous period.</p>
<p>Outstanding borrowing via the discount facility and swaps of money market certificates fell by 48.2 million francs to 1,083.6 million.</p>
<p>An SNB spokesman said that the latest 10-day statement showed sight deposits were relatively high. But he said the increase in the latest period was due mainly to normal month- end demand, amplified by the fact it was also quarter-end.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
